{
  "description": "#6099 — a move into another space refuses, whole and changing nothing, a page title or tag name a live page or tag of that space holds, as a rename does; so does the move's undo. The ops make three spaces, Home (`C1`), Work (`C3`) and an empty Archive (`C8`), a `Work` tag in Home (`C2`), an `Inbox` page in Work (`C4`) and one in Home (`C7`), a `work` tag (`C5`) and a `Plan` page (`C6`) in Work. Moving `Inbox` into Home is refused with `DuplicatePageTitle`, and so is moving `Plan` and `Inbox` together, so `Plan` stays too; moving `work` is refused under the tag fold. `Plan` alone moves into Archive (O32). Once Work has a new `Plan` (`C9`), undoing O32 is refused the same way. The snapshot carries no `space_id`, so a refused move shows as ranks that did not change and ops that were not appended. Re-author `expected` / `expected_ops` via CONFORMANCE_UPDATE=1.",
